## What to deliver

Build and rig the mech up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: an upright body with a head on top, two
articulated legs planted beneath it, and a heavy rail-lance cannon mounted on one
shoulder — seated on a structural turret mount bolted to the frame, machinery built
onto the chassis, with no hand and no gripping arm. **Author the two required
animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation subcommands: a playable
**`walk`** (the two legs striding in opposite phase, each foot planting flat and still
then lifting and swinging — with weight, not a weightless slide) and a weapon-only
**`fire`** recoil (the whole cannon kicking straight back along its own axis in its
shoulder mount, then settling, while the legs hold their stance). The animations are
the fixed contract —
produce both, by those names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. When
you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished
submission.
